ragement  although he would never go to space  himself von braun is responsible for  getting the first humans to the moon on  the apollo 11 mission in 1969  at the time the american public knew  very little if anything about his past  as a member of the nazi party and an ss  officer there was no existing photo of  von braun in which you can clearly see  him in his uniform the closest is this  photo of him wearing the nazi party  badge on his suit lapel although even  this isn't all that clear the us  government largely hid his background  until after his death he was among  hundreds of german scientists engineers  and technicians recruited as part of  operation paperclip at the end of world  war ii although president truman forbade  recruiting nazi members or supporters  u.s intelligence agencies eliminated or  whitewashed incriminating evidence of  possible war crimes from their records  one brown was the star recruit he was  the brains behind the nazis v2 ballistic  missile the first object to go into  space defined as 62 vertical miles out  or 100 kilometers and effectively  launched the space age von braun led the  team that developed the v2 at a secret  laboratory at pinamunda located on a  northern german island from there they  built and tested the rockets by  launching them into the baltic sea  the v in v2 stands for the german word  vergel tongswaffen which means vengeance  this was vengeance weapon number two  v2s attacked allied cities in  retaliation for the allied bombings  against german cities  they were used in the latter stages of  the war and were a last-ditch effort by  the germans to ward off defeat the v2  was a totally new kind of weapon it was  the world's first large-scale liquid  propellant rocket instead of weapons  with a hundred pounds of thrust it had  55 000 pounds of thrust the nazis  launched over 3000 v2s equipped with a  one-ton warhead targeting western europe  mostly britain and belgium they flew at  more than 3 000 miles an hour or 4 800  kilometers an hour and could reach  london in five minutes because they came  in at over three times the speed of  sound the v2 made absolutely no sound  until after it hit so it crashed and  exploded without warning it is estimated  to have killed between 5 000 to 9 000  civilians and soldiers yet more than  twice as many people are believed to  have died producing them the nazis  forced prisoners from concentration  camps to build the rockets at the  middlework factory underneath a mountain  in central germany to avoid enemy air  attacks prisoners did 12 hours a day of  back-breaking work pushing heavy  equipment in areas filled with dust and  noxious gases from the blasting to widen  the tunnels conditions were far worse  than depicted in this nazi propaganda  photo they slept in the tunnels they dug  their only toilets or oil barrels cut in  half with boards over them because there  wasn't enough many relieved themselves  in the tunnels the stench was  intolerable starvation and poor hygiene  exacerbated outbreaks of typhoid and  tuberculosis the nazis recruited  prisoners who had technical skills such  as welding to build the rockets those  accused of sabotaging their production  were hanged from cranes above the rocket  assembly lines when von braun was later  asked by a reporter if he was aware of  the slave labor that built the v2s he  said well you're misinformed the slave  camp was about 400 miles from where i  worked i learned later on that there  were atrocities taking place there but i  was not involved in this whole operation  i have nothing to hide i have nothing to  hide  however historians are certain von braun  saw the horrific conditions with his own  eyes michael j neufeld author of the  book von braun dreamer of space engineer  of war found through his research that  von braun was in the tunnels at least a  dozen times newfeld said that when von  braun testified at a war crimes trial in  west germany in the late 60s he  mentioned he'd 