lar opposites one was part  of hitler's inhumanity  the other a giant leap for humanity  it's easy to label someone a hero or a  villain to see things as black and white  but real life is complicated and so was  von braun  what was clear is that above all else  von braun loved space  while a student he read an article  imagining a trip to the moon and  recalled it filled me with a romantic  urge interplanetary travel here was a  task worth dedicating one's life to not  just stare through a telescope at the  moon in the planets but to soar through  the heavens and actually explore the  mysterious universe i knew how columbus  had felt  von braun achieved his dream because of  his determination to master calculus and  trigonometry so he could understand the  physics of rocketry if you'd like to  improve your stem skills brilliant is my  go-to platform to improve my critical  thinking and problem-solving skills and  it's free for you to try out i know my  viewers love the scientific thinking  course where you can explore the laws of  physics and the principles of  engineering by learning as you play i  really like that it's super interactive  there's something for everyone on  brilliant no matter your age or  experience level you can start your  algebra journey with an introduction to  variables and equations with their  pre-algebra course or begin your math  journey by seeing fractions percents and  ratios in everyday contexts with their  everyday math course if you're ever  stuck on a problem you can view the  explanation for more brilliant is free  for you to try out if you head to my  custom link brilliant.org newsthink  which is in my description and the first  200 people who sign up with my link will  get 20 off brilliant's annual premium  subscription which gives you access to  all of their course offerings  thanks for watching for newsthink i'm  cindy palm

